                <pb facs="0746" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.852/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-18T00:00:00-04:00">June 18,
                        1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1588. Department’s 1500, June 11, 10 p.m. Mr. Myron L. Black and Mr. Jack C.
                    Corbett representing the War Shipping Administration and the Department,
                    respectively, will depart from Miami by plane on June 20 for Rio. Mr. E. G.
                    Rose, War Shipping Administration’s <pb facs="0747" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>
                    marine surveyor, will arrive sometime later from Venezuela.</p>
                <p>Please arrange for single room accommodations at Copacabana-Palace for Black and
                    Corbett.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
